  "body": "## Summary\nThe validatePrice() function in UniswapPriceOracle.sol contains a mathematical error \nwhere the calculated TWAP always equals the current spot price, rendering the \nslippage protection completely ineffective.\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\nThe function attempts to calculate a Time-Weighted Average Price (TWAP) to compare \nagainst the current spot price:\n\nsolidity\nuint256 cumulativePrice = cumulativePriceLast + (tradePrice * elapsedTime);\nuint256 timeWeightedAverage = (cumulativePrice - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime;\n\n\nMathematical simplification:\ntimeWeightedAverage = (cumulativePriceLast + tradePrice * elapsedTime - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime\n                    = (tradePrice * elapsedTime) / elapsedTime\n                    = tradePrice\n\n\nSince timeWeightedAverage == tradePrice, the derivation calculation always returns 0:\nsolidity\nuint256 derivation = (tradePrice > timeWeightedAverage)\n    ? ((tradePrice - timeWeightedAverage) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage\n    : ((timeWeightedAverage - tradePrice) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage;\n// derivation = 0 always\n\n\nThis means validatePrice() always returns true regardless of price manipulation.\n\n## Impact\n\nHIGH - The slippage protection in BuyBackBurner._buyOLAS() is ineffective:\n\n1. Attacker flash loans tokens and manipulates Uniswap V2 pool price\n2. Calls buyBack() on BuyBackBurner\n3. validatePrice(maxSlippage) passes (TWAP = manipulated spot price)\n4. previousPrice captures the manipulated price\n5. Swap executes at unfavorable rate\n6. Post-swap check compares against already-manipulated previousPrice, so it passes\n7. Protocol loses funds to sandwich attack\n\nAffected functions:\n- BuyBackBurner.sol:185 - pre-swap validation\n- LiquidityManagerETH.sol:170\n- LiquidityManagerOptimism.sol:232",
  "proof_of_concept": "solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.28;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\n// Minimal mock of Uniswap V2 pair\ncontract MockUniswapV2Pair {\n    uint112 public reserve0 = 1000e18;\n    uint112 public reserve1 = 1000e18;\n    uint256 public price0CumulativeLast = 1000e18;\n    uint256 public price1CumulativeLast = 1000e18;\n    uint32 public blockTimestampLast;\n    address public token0 = address(0x1);\n\n    constructor() {\n        blockTimestampLast = uint32(block.timestamp - 100);\n    }\n\n    function getReserves() external view returns (uint112, uint112, uint32) {\n        return (reserve0, reserve1, blockTimestampLast);\n    }\n\n    function manipulatePrice(uint112 newReserve0, uint112 newReserve1) external {\n        reserve0 = newReserve0;\n        reserve1 = newReserve1;\n    }\n}\n\n// Copy of vulnerable contract\ncontract UniswapPriceOracle {\n    address public immutable pair;\n    uint256 public immutable maxSlippage;\n    uint256 public immutable direction;\n\n    constructor(address _secondToken, uint256 _maxSlippage, address _pair) {\n        pair = _pair;\n        maxSlippage = _maxSlippage;\n        address token0 = MockUniswapV2Pair(_pair).token0();\n        if (token0 != _secondToken) {\n            direction = 1;\n        }\n    }\n\n    function getPrice() public view returns (uint256) {\n        (uint112 r0, uint112 r1,) = MockUniswapV2Pair(pair).getReserves();\n        uint256 balanceIn = direction == 0 ? r0 : r1;\n        uint256 balanceOut = direction == 0 ? r1 : r0;\n        return (balanceOut * 1e18) / balanceIn;\n    }\n\n    function validatePrice(uint256 slippage) external view returns (bool) {\n        require(slippage <= maxSlippage, \"Slippage overflow\");\n\n        uint256 cumulativePriceLast = direction == 0 \n            ? MockUniswapV2Pair(pair).price1CumulativeLast()\n            : MockUniswapV2Pair(pair).price0CumulativeLast();\n\n        (,, uint32 blockTimestampLast) =